;; Signals only within this sandbox. Under (allow default) a sandboxed process
;; can signal every process of the same user. Shown: Hermes in the sandbox
;; listed the host's own Hermes gateway by PID (`hermes gateway status`), and
;; `hermes gateway run --replace` would stop such a process. This rule keeps
;; signals inside the sandbox. NOT yet probed across the boundary: that probe
;; moves to the macOS VM work. Shown only that the sandbox still stops its own
;; children (gateway shutdown, run-capped.sh cleanup from outside).
(deny signal (with message (param "SANDBOX_TAG")))
(allow signal (target same-sandbox))
